# Line endings are law for what the suite reads as TEXT (prd-25 ruling 4, #210).
#
# The era corpus reaches @rhizomorph/core as `?raw` text through
# packages/core/src/eras/corpus.ts, and the golden-era law compares the fold to
# the committed snapshot byte for byte. Under core.autocrlf=true — the
# Git-for-Windows default — a checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, so the INPUT lies
# and nothing inside the suite can repair it: the corpus cannot be re-blessed
# from inside vitest by design (eras.test.ts). The same failure reaches every
# JSON / JSONL / text fixture a collector test reads off disk. The only native
# Windows run this project has ever done lost the eras golden byte-identity to
# exactly this.
#
# packages/server/src/corpus-eol-law.test.ts asks `git check-attr` about every
# file the suite reads as text and fails if one is not covered here. Nothing
# below renormalised a committed byte: every pinned file was already LF (or a
# single line with no line ending) in the index when this landed.
*.jsonl                                        text eol=lf
*.json                                         text eol=lf
packages/server/src/collectors/*/fixtures/**   text eol=lf
